  "title": "Dr Reddy's receives DCGI nod for cancer drug's second indication in India",
  "summary": "Dr Reddy's Laboratories received approval from the Drugs Controller General of India (DCGI) for Zytorvi, a monoclonal antibody designed to target PD-1 and PD-L1 in advanced esophageal cancer. The approval expands its use to combine with cisplatin and paclitaxel for first-line treatment of unresectable ESCC patients. This marks Zytorvi's second approval in India, expanding beyond nasopharyngeal carcinoma.",
