    {
      "title": "Dr Reddy's receives DCGI approval for esophageal cancer drug Zytorvi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/dr-reddy-s-receives-dcgi-approval-for-esophageal-cancer-drug-zytorvi-126102100323_1.html",
      "description": "Dr Reddy's Laboratories on Wednesday said it has received approval from the Drugs Controller General of India (DCGI) for Zytorvi (toripalimab), through which it aims to expand access to first-line immunotherapy for patients with advanced esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC) in India.\nThe drug has been approved in combination with cisplatin and paclitaxel for the first-line treatment of adult patients with unresectable advanced, recurrent, or metastatic ESCC, the pharma company said in a release.\nThis marks Zytorvi's second approved indication in the country, expanding beyond nasopharyngeal carcinoma.\nESCC accounts for approximately 80 per cent of all esophageal cancer cases in India, the company said.\nZytorvi contains toripalimab, a monoclonal antibody that binds to PD-1 and blocks its interaction with PD-L1 and PD-L2, thereby supporting T-cell activity against cancer cells.\nThe approval is supported by results from the Phase 3 JUPITER-06 trial. In the study, toripalimab in .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-21T06:27:32"
    }
